issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**
STM32 SPI DMA client can work with TX and RX, or TX/RX only configuration.
Configuration should be done using device tree:
```
&spi1 {
	dmas = <&dmamux1 11 7 0x20440 0
		&dmamux1 1 6 0x20480 0>;
	dma-names = "tx", "rx";
};
```
Tx only configuration
```
&spi1 {
	dmas = <&dmamux1 11 7 0x20440 0>;
	dma-names = "tx";
};
```
Both configs above work fine, but SPI driver does not compile in RX only configuration.

**To Reproduce**
Build `tests/drivers/spi/spi_loopback/` and tweak `boards/nucleo_wb55rg.overlay`

**Expected behavior**
SPI DMA client can build in all single channel config
